unknown_openers
  summary "The deterministic opener pools the unknown-intent fallback varies over (issue #144), moved out of Rust and JavaScript constants into seed data by issue #706. A pool belongs to the language slug registered in 'language-detection.lino'; the first opener of a pool must equal the opener already embedded in that language's 'unknown' response in 'multilingual-responses.lino', so the varied answer stays a strict superset of the seed text. Adding a language's openers is a data edit shared by the Rust core, the no_std WASM worker, and the JS worker."
  fallback_language en
  pool
    language en
    opener "I don't know how to answer that yet."
    opener "I didn't understand you."
    opener "I'm not sure how to respond to that yet."
    opener "I haven't learned to answer that yet."
    opener "That one is new to me."
  pool
    language ru
    opener "Я пока не знаю, как ответить на это."
    opener "Я тебя не понял."
    opener "Я не уверен, как на это ответить."
    opener "Я ещё не научился отвечать на это."
    opener "Это для меня новое."
  pool
    language hi
    opener "मुझे अभी इसका उत्तर देना नहीं आता।"
    opener "मैं समझ नहीं पाया।"
    opener "मुझे यकीन नहीं है कि कैसे उत्तर दूँ।"
    opener "मैंने अभी तक यह उत्तर देना नहीं सीखा।"
    opener "यह मेरे लिए नया है।"
  pool
    language zh
    opener "我还不知道如何回答这个问题。"
    opener "我不太明白你说的意思。"
    opener "我不确定该如何回答。"
    opener "我还没有学会回答这个问题。"
    opener "这对我来说是新的。"
  sentence_separator ". "
  sentence_separator "。"
  sentence_separator "। "
